# Type labels (Projects + Insights)

On `.projects-page`, `.project-detail`, `.insights-page`, `.insight-detail`:

1. **No fill** — no border, background, or capsule padding on type labels.
2. **Font** — SF Pro Display Medium (`var(--font-sans)`, weight `500`) — same as filter pills. CSS: `--font-type-label`.
3. **Size** — shared `--type-chip-font` (current size, −3% recipe). Same everywhere: featured, cards, Related, case hero tag.
4. **Color** — gray (`--type-label-color`, ~50% white).
5. **Title + description** in card/lead meta — **white** (`#fff`).
6. **Top-align with title** — every type label (and its chip list wrapper) uses `align-self: start` / `align-items: start`. Never baseline or vertical-center labels against titles.

Applies to `.project-type-chip`, `.insight-chip`, `.project-case-demo__tag`.

Filter involvement pills are separate UI — not this recipe.

# Featured / case hero meta (desktop)

**Scope:** `.project-featured__meta`, `.insights-lead__meta`, and `.project-case-demo__hero-copy` (desktop). Same recipe.

1. Type label `max-content`, **end-aligned**, top-aligned.
2. Description **left-aligned with** centered `.site-nav` (primary links). `--site-nav-inset` / `--site-nav-half` from Header.
3. Title → description gap: **5.5vw**.
4. Description → tag gap: **10vw**; description takes the remaining width between nav-left and that spacer.
5. Title size: shared `--project-meta-title-size`.

Do **not** apply this recipe to filter/Related cards.

# Filter / Related cards

Title up to **65%** | type label end-aligned / top-aligned | description full width under. Label **size** still comes from the unified tokens above.

# Featured lead meta (mobile ≤800px)

`.project-featured__meta` and `.insights-lead__meta` match the filter card stack (not the desktop nav-align recipe):

1. Title ≤ **65%** | type label **end-aligned / top-aligned**.
2. Description on the next row, **full** card width, left-aligned.

Leads stay visible above the filter on mobile (do not hide).

# Project detail hero meta (mobile ≤800px)

`.project-case-demo__hero-copy` matches the card stack (not the desktop nav-align recipe):

1. Title ≤ **65%** | type label **end-aligned / top-aligned** (gap between).
2. Description on the next row, **full** usable width, left-aligned.
